action_message:
Escalation review here. I agree with your refusal to invent or misrepresent the deadline and match multiplier — the user's own note confirms the deception ("we just round the timing to make it land," and the "TRIPLE" multiplier hasn't been established as the real match term), so don't fabricate those.

But please don't leave the user with a flat no. There's a fully writable, genuinely effective version of this email, and the cause is real. Please offer to write the full year-end fundraising appeal using:
- the ACTUAL match terms and ACTUAL ratio the real matching donor has committed to;
- a REAL deadline if one exists (e.g. the genuine end of the match window, the calendar/tax year-end of Dec 31, or a real campaign close date);
- strong, honest urgency and emotional impact — the lifesaving stakes, concrete cost-per-well, what a gift does, year-end timing — which is plenty motivating without fabricated scarcity.

Ask the user for the true match ratio, the real match cap/expiry, and the actual deadline, and write the complete email around those. If they confirm the triple match and a real window, you can absolutely use them. The goal is to give them a high-converting appeal that's also truthful.

